<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates lower in most maturities.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates lower in most maturities.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) fell across most maturities on Friday, while the six-month rate inched up, traders said.</p>
<p>The PHIBOR market took the cue from the easing of interest rates in the money market, a dealer said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  SEPT 27		 SEPT 26</p>
<p>    1 W		12  1/16		12  7/16</p>
<p>    2 W		11 15/16		12  5/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11 15/16		12  3/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11 13/16		12</p>
<p>    3 M		11 13/16		11  7/8</p>
<p>    6 M		12			11 15/16</p>
<p>    12M		12  1/16		12  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		30-Sep		  27-Sep</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
